Subject: man grep only mentions egrep and fgrep

The manpage should mention all grep variants, like rgrep.

Reported-by: Goswin Brederlow <goswin.brederlow@student.uni-tuebingen.de>
Bug-Debian: http://bugs.debian.org/127438
---
 doc/grep.1 |   12 ++++++++----
 1 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/doc/grep.1 b/doc/grep.1
index 950b82c..2aaf290 100644
--- a/doc/grep.1
+++ b/doc/grep.1
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 .hy 0
 .
 .SH NAME
-grep, egrep, fgrep \- print lines matching a pattern
+grep, egrep, fgrep, rgrep \- print lines matching a pattern
 .
 .SH SYNOPSIS
 .B grep
@@ -57,10 +57,11 @@ By default,
 .B grep
 prints the matching lines.
 .PP
-In addition, two variant programs
-.B egrep
-and
+In addition, three variant programs
+.B egrep,
 .B fgrep
+and
+.B rgrep
 are available.
 .B egrep
 is the same as
@@ -68,6 +69,9 @@ is the same as
 .B fgrep
 is the same as
 .BR "grep\ \-F" .
+.B rgrep
+is the same as
+.BR "grep\ \-r" .
 Direct invocation as either
 .B egrep
